WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:04.200
UIPrism takes a screenshot, URL, repo or Figma file as input

00:04.700 --> 00:07.800
The starting point is a screenshot of an existing interface

00:09.400 --> 00:13.400
Here: a finished sustainability dashboard

00:14.300 --> 00:18.200
Import by drag and drop

00:19.000 --> 00:22.400
The AI reads out colors, typography, spacing and components

00:22.900 --> 00:25.600
Import complete: 23 tokens, 19 components

00:26.100 --> 00:30.000
The tokens: colors, typography, spacing, radius, shadows

00:30.500 --> 00:34.300
Then the components, atoms first

00:34.900 --> 00:39.000
Each component with its origin in the layout and its mapping to shadcn/ui

00:39.600 --> 00:43.600
Preview directly in the list

00:44.200 --> 00:47.600
Atoms, molecules, organisms, templates

00:48.000 --> 00:50.000
… with ready-to-use JSX code

00:50.500 --> 00:54.200
Targets: Figma, Storybook or the whole library

00:54.700 --> 00:58.200
An empty Figma file, plus the UIPrism plugin

00:58.700 --> 01:03.100
Scan and export: color and text styles are created

01:03.600 --> 01:08.800
The components are created directly in the file

01:09.300 --> 01:14.900
Atoms, molecules and organisms as real Figma components

01:15.400 --> 01:20.900
… and assemble into the dashboard layout

01:21.400 --> 01:27.900
Done: 10 colors, 5 text styles, 19 components, 1 template

01:28.700 --> 01:31.900
One click: “Open in Storybook”

01:32.400 --> 01:36.900
Storybook with all detected components

01:37.400 --> 01:42.600
Every component with variants and controls

01:43.200 --> 01:49.800
Up to the finished dashboard template in the browser

01:50.100 --> 01:55.800
One screenshot → design tokens, code, Figma library and Storybook
